🔴 Description

It was observed that the application stores encrypted credential files (.enc) along with corresponding key and IV files (.txt) within the same accessible directory path. The files are available in a shared network location used by the Excel add-in. This implementation exposes all required components needed to decrypt sensitive credentials. Storing encryption keys together with encrypted data defeats the purpose of encryption and indicates improper key management.

🔴 Impact
Attackers with access to the directory can decrypt credentials and gain unauthorized access to databases/services
Leads to compromise of sensitive financial or market data handled by the application
Increases risk of privilege escalation and lateral movement across environments
🔧 Mitigation
It is recommended to implement secure key management by storing encryption keys separately in a protected key vault or HSM instead of local/shared directories
Restrict access to credential files using least privilege and remove exposure from shared network paths
Use strong encryption practices with proper key rotation and ensure keys are never stored alongside encrypted data
